
☐ registry virtualisation of hklm is broken; writes go directly to the real reg

☐ Delete logic: NtDeleteKey/NtDeleteValueKey only deletes from virtual store - this is a known bug area: if a real-only key is "deleted", it reappears after re-open because there's no tombstone mechanism for registry keys (unlike files).
☐ NtQueryKey: Returns virtual key metadata (subkey count, value count from virtual only, not merged count - possible bug).
☐ NtQueryMultipleValueKey: Tries virtual entirely, falls back to real if fails - but doesn't do per-value fallback (possible bug).

::    - No registry tombstone: deleting a real-only key / value inside the
::      sandbox does NOT persist -- the real key reappears on re-open.
::      (File virtualisation uses .vl_deleted tombstones; registry does not.)
::    - NtQueryKey reports virtual-only subkey/value counts, not merged.
::    - NtQueryMultipleValueKey is all-or-nothing (no per-value fallback).


